1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:04,389
Unit Alerts helps a coordination team find
units that have remained in a timed

2
00:00:04,389 --> 00:00:06,860
status longer than the department expects.

3
00:00:07,269 --> 00:00:11,979
In Big Board, use the plus icon and choose
Unit Alerts from Add Widget.

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:13,699
Scroll to the new panel.

5
00:00:14,170 --> 00:00:17,729
This department initially shows No status
timers configured.

6
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:22,620
That message describes the missing timer
configuration; it does not establish

7
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:24,780
that every unit has reported promptly.

8
00:00:25,139 --> 00:00:28,579
The thresholds are department settings
managed in the Core website.

9
00:00:28,829 --> 00:00:33,300
In Core, open Department Settings, choose
Operations, then

10
00:00:33,370 --> 00:00:35,089
Mapping and BigBoard Settings.

11
00:00:35,479 --> 00:00:37,589
Scroll to Unit Status Timers.

12
00:00:37,999 --> 00:00:43,230
The table separates Status, Warn after in
minutes, and Alert after in minutes.

13
00:00:43,579 --> 00:00:47,199
Each displayed status has its own row,
including Dispatched,

14
00:00:47,369 --> 00:00:49,980
Responding, En Route and On Scene.

15
00:00:50,390 --> 00:00:53,800
Initially, both columns are zero
throughout this training table.

16
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:57,879
The helper text explains that leaving both
at zero times nothing.

17
00:00:58,289 --> 00:01:01,209
Choose values that fit your department's
reporting process.

18
00:01:01,419 --> 00:01:06,390
For this software exercise, enter two
under Warn after and four under

19
00:01:06,419 --> 00:01:08,510
Alert after on the Responding row.

20
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:10,679
Leave the other rows unchanged.

21
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:14,839
These are demonstration values, not a
recommended response standard.

22
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:19,159
The two columns allow the department to
distinguish a warning interval from a

23
00:01:19,159 --> 00:01:21,790
later alert interval for the same status.

24
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:26,739
Review the row label and both minute
values before saving, so the timer applies

25
00:01:26,739 --> 00:01:28,620
to the intended operational meaning.

26
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:32,510
Below the table, set Reason when
acknowledging to Required

27
00:01:32,510 --> 00:01:33,959
for warnings and alerts.

28
00:01:34,399 --> 00:01:37,610
The help explains that this policy applies
when acknowledging

29
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,600
or muting a status timer alert.

30
00:01:40,070 --> 00:01:41,129
Select Save.

31
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:44,830
Reload Mapping and BigBoard Settings and
return to the table:

32
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:47,599
Responding still shows two and four.

33
00:01:48,029 --> 00:01:51,429
Scroll down again and verify the
required-reason selection.

34
00:01:51,929 --> 00:01:55,699
Reading back both controls checks the
saved configuration before you

35
00:01:55,699 --> 00:01:57,410
examine its effect in Big Board.

36
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:58,720
Reload Big Board.

37
00:01:59,229 --> 00:02:04,400
Unit Alerts now shows Squad Three, its
Responding state, Firehouse Fifty One

38
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:06,339
and the elapsed time in that state.

39
00:02:06,759 --> 00:02:10,459
This fictional record is already more than
one hundred eighty hours

40
00:02:10,459 --> 00:02:15,640
old, far beyond the four-minute alert
threshold, so it appears red immediately.

41
00:02:16,089 --> 00:02:19,550
The elapsed value helps identify a status
report needing review.

42
00:02:19,929 --> 00:02:22,210
It does not explain why the report is old.

43
00:02:22,649 --> 00:02:26,589
Use the unit's normal reporting and
coordination process to investigate.

44
00:02:26,790 --> 00:02:30,120
Select the Squad Three row to open Unit
status alert.

45
00:02:30,489 --> 00:02:33,629
With Reason empty, the sheet explains the
requirement and

46
00:02:33,629 --> 00:02:35,430
disables Acknowledge and Mute.

47
00:02:35,829 --> 00:02:39,720
Enter the clearly labeled training reason,
then select Acknowledge.

48
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:40,999
Reopen the row.

49
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:46,289
The saved section now says Seen by Wallace
Boden and retains the exercise note.

50
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:51,039
Acknowledging records that review; the
unit still has its Responding state.

51
00:02:51,410 --> 00:02:54,560
The sheet also offers Clear
acknowledgement for removing

52
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:55,709
the saved acknowledgement.

53
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:59,419
If the small alert panel clips the saved
note, open the gear

54
00:02:59,419 --> 00:03:01,700
settings and select Unit Alerts.

55
00:03:02,079 --> 00:03:07,129
Under Widget Size, this example uses width
four and height three grid units.

56
00:03:07,489 --> 00:03:09,619
Select Save and return to the panel.

57
00:03:10,039 --> 00:03:14,430
The wider, taller result shows the unit,
state, reviewer and

58
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:16,049
complete training note together.

59
00:03:16,489 --> 00:03:20,540
Reopening these settings after a later
reload still shows four by three.

60
00:03:20,919 --> 00:03:24,309
Check the rendered result as well as the
values in the editing form.

61
00:03:24,509 --> 00:03:26,050
Open the same alert again.

62
00:03:26,470 --> 00:03:29,309
Under Mute for, select fifteen minutes.

63
00:03:29,690 --> 00:03:32,420
Replace the reason with the note
describing this fictional

64
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,940
mute exercise, then choose Mute.

65
00:03:35,389 --> 00:03:38,589
The panel now has a collapsed Muted, one,
section.

66
00:03:38,990 --> 00:03:42,199
Expand it to see Squad Three and the saved
mute reason.

67
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:44,420
The unit still says Responding.

68
00:03:44,830 --> 00:03:49,520
Moving an alert into this section changes
how the timer alert is presented; it does

69
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,850
not resolve the underlying unit state.

70
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:57,050
Reload Big Board, expand Muted, one, and
reopen Squad Three.

71
00:03:57,559 --> 00:04:01,899
The sheet retains the reviewer and reason
and displays a Muted until time.

72
00:04:02,350 --> 00:04:05,069
This checks that the saved mute survived a
reload.

73
00:04:05,529 --> 00:04:08,420
For this exercise, choose Clear
acknowledgement.

74
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:11,879
The unit returns to the active red alert
panel, because its

75
00:04:11,950 --> 00:04:15,600
unchanged Responding record is still
beyond the configured threshold.

76
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:20,120
The timer, saved acknowledgement or mute,
and underlying unit status

77
00:04:20,170 --> 00:04:21,819
are separate things to verify.

78
00:04:22,029 --> 00:04:26,739
A security control room can use status
timers to review a delayed patrol update.

79
00:04:27,190 --> 00:04:30,659
Search-and-rescue coordinators can follow
a team's reporting interval.

80
00:04:31,119 --> 00:04:34,869
Community paramedicine and mental health
response teams, wildland

81
00:04:34,869 --> 00:04:39,870
contractors, industrial response teams,
and fire and E M S departments can

82
00:04:39,870 --> 00:04:43,860
apply the same review process with
appropriate statuses and thresholds.

83
00:04:44,239 --> 00:04:48,120
Configure the timer, inspect the actual
unit and elapsed time,

84
00:04:48,569 --> 00:04:52,280
document the review, and verify the saved
result using fictional

85
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:54,470
data before adopting the process.

